    "text": "By Bailey Stamos, WRAL reporter ,\n5 hours ago Leah Wright remembers the moment she received the call that no parent wants to answer. She learned her son, 28-year-old Carrson Kase Wilson, had died. Leah and Jimmy Wright founded Wake Monarch Academy in Raleigh in 2021, the first recovery-focused high school. In fact, the \"why\" behind the passion project started with Carrson, after his struggle with addiction. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
